    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "lines": [
        "Frost Heave Under Lightweight Footbridges: A Field Study of Three Timber Crossings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "Maren Solberg¹, Pieter Achterberg² and Lucia Ferrante¹"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "address",
      "lines": [
        "¹Department of Civil Engineering, Fjordvik University, Norway",
        "²Delta Structural Monitoring BV, Delft, the Netherlands"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "address",
      "lines": [
        "{m.solberg, l.ferrante}@fjordvik.example"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "Abstract—Short-span timber footbridges on shallow pad foundations are often built on frost-susceptible soils. We monitored three crossings in central Norway through two winters and found seasonal heave of 8 to 15 mm at the abutments, enough to open the deck joints and tilt the handrail posts. Heave tracked the square root of the frost index closely, and a simple coefficient fitted at one site predicted the other two within 2 mm."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "lines": [
        "I. Introduction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "Most footbridges built by small municipalities are light timber structures",
        "with a single span of 15 to 35 m. Their foundations are chosen for cost, and",
        "where the ground freezes, pad footings above the frost line are common.¹",
        "The resulting movement is rarely measured, although it is a frequent cause of",
        "maintenance calls."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "lines": [
        "III. RESULTS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "Heave began within a week of the first sustained frost and peaked in late",
        "February at all three sites. Fig. 1 shows the mean heave by month, and Table I",
        "summarises each crossing."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "This paper reports two winters of monitoring at three such crossings and"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "proposes a one-parameter model for the heave of their abutments."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "lines": [
        "II. METHOD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "Each abutment carried two survey targets read weekly with a total station.",
        "Air temperature was logged hourly, and the frost index F was taken as the",
        "sum of daily mean temperatures below zero. We fitted the relation",
        "Δh = α √F",
        "(1)",
        "where Δh is the heave in millimetres and α a site coefficient."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "caption",
      "lines": [
        "Fig. 1. Mean abutment heave by month, November to April."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "lines": [
        "'The national guidance permits this where",
        "the span is under 40 m and the deck is not",
        "continuous over the supports."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        "With α fitted at Brekke, (1) predicted the peak heave at the other two sites",
        "within 2 mm."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
